                <pb facs="0410" n="396" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg396"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.731/36: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-01T19:00:00-04:00">March 1, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>363. Reference your no. 598, March 1. If you deem it necessary you may inform the
                    All America Cables Company that you have been authorized by the Department to
                    request that all copies of Embassy’s cables be returned to the Embassy to insure
                    adequate protection and security.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
